Full table: `docs/language/import-style.md`

## New packages

1. Run `./scripts/li-new-package --import-name physics.foo --official` (creates `packages/li-physics-foo`)
2. Or run `scripts/apply-import-names.py` / `align-package-repo-names.py` on existing packages
3. Set `github_repo` + `import_name` in `li.toml` (see `docs/ecosystem/repo-naming.md`)
3. Add `std/physics/foo.li` facade (tag proc or re-export)
4. Register in `packages/li.toml` workspace `members`

## Agents

- Refactor docs/samples to ergonomic imports when touching a file
- Prefer extending `easy_std_module()` in `import_resolve.cpp` over new top-level prefixes
- Keep **one concern per module** — `physics.em` not `physics.em_fdtd_waveguide`
